1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:08,968
You really can't help flirting
with my husband, huh?

2
00:00:09,051 --> 00:00:11,387
I get it! You're rich and pretty!

3
00:00:11,470 --> 00:00:13,097
But you're so insecure!

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,641
Ana hired me to be a loyalty tester.

5
00:00:15,725 --> 00:00:17,393
To find out if you're having an affair.

6
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:19,270
<i>That was unnecessary, Ana.</i>

7
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:22,773
<i>There are just so many things</i>
<i>about you that I don't get.</i>

8
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:27,027
<i>And all of this happened</i>
<i>just because of loyalty testing.</i>

9
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:28,738
Are you seriously
blaming Ana for getting upset

10
00:00:28,821 --> 00:00:30,114
when you flirted with her husband?

11
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:31,282
I don't care!

12
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,033
I love Ben.

13
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:35,035
Are you finally awake?

14
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:38,164
You can reach all you want,

15
00:00:38,247 --> 00:00:42,376
but you will never ever touch what's mine.

16
00:00:43,294 --> 00:00:44,545
Please help me.

17
00:00:44,628 --> 00:00:46,213
I'm begging you.

18
00:00:46,297 --> 00:00:48,299
<i>Congratulations, Attorney!</i>

19
00:00:48,382 --> 00:00:51,302
<i>I mean... sorry, Mr. CEO.</i>

20
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:52,928
<i>Wow!</i>

21
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:54,805
What are you doing here?

22
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:57,308
Ben, I'm here to talk to you.

23
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,674
Ben, where are you?

24
00:02:11,757 --> 00:02:13,676
You said you would be right back.

25
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:16,136
<i>Hello, love.</i>

26
00:02:17,096 --> 00:02:19,431
<i>I'm sorry I didn't update you right away.</i>

27
00:02:19,974 --> 00:02:22,059
<i>I had to attend to an emergency.</i>

28
00:02:23,018 --> 00:02:25,688
Okay, well...

29
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:27,648
Just... come back when you can.

30
00:02:27,731 --> 00:02:29,441
<i>Yeah, I'll let you know.</i>

31
00:02:29,525 --> 00:02:30,860
<i>I love you. Bye.</i>

32
00:02:30,943 --> 00:02:31,986
Okay, bye.

33
00:02:44,748 --> 00:02:48,419
What happened to that, Ging?

34
00:02:49,003 --> 00:02:50,254
That wasn't me.

35
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:55,301
Ging, what happened to this?

36
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,511
It wasn't me.

37
00:02:57,595 --> 00:03:00,222
How could I do that? I was tied up.

38
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:03,684
Who did it, then?

39
00:03:06,562 --> 00:03:08,272
There was a woman.

40
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:12,318
A woman?

41
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:16,113
There was a woman
who wanted to help me.

42
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,658
At least someone cares about me.

43
00:03:21,243 --> 00:03:24,163
A woman came here and broke that window?

44
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:27,791
Yes. There was a woman there
before you arrived.

45
00:03:30,044 --> 00:03:31,211
Ging.

46
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:35,132
Are you telling the truth?

47
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,726
What did she look like?

48
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,362
What did she look like, Ging?

49
00:03:58,322 --> 00:04:00,783
There was a woman there
before you arrived.

50
00:04:14,797 --> 00:04:16,382


51
00:04:19,093 --> 00:04:20,678
Stay here, okay?

52
00:04:22,972 --> 00:04:24,431
Ging, don't go anywhere.

53
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:33,524


54
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:52,519

That woman you slapped at the café...

55
00:05:52,936 --> 00:05:56,023
is it the same woman
who caused a scene at my house?

56
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:57,149
How do you--

57
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:59,651
Ana, people are talking.

58
00:05:59,735 --> 00:06:01,195
So, am I right?

59
00:06:03,072 --> 00:06:04,823
-
Am I right?

60
00:06:04,907 --> 00:06:06,575
She's Mariano's physical therapist.

61
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:09,661
And now, she's your husband's
physical therapist too.

62
00:06:10,454 --> 00:06:11,622
Yes.

63
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:14,249
But Ma, you don't need
to know these things.

64
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:16,085
Ben and I are okay now.

65
00:06:17,044 --> 00:06:18,045
Are you sure?

66
00:06:18,128 --> 00:06:19,588
Yes, I'm sure.

67
00:06:20,506 --> 00:06:22,508

You know what I'm curious about?

68
00:06:22,591 --> 00:06:26,220
How did she end up being a homewrecker?

69
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,930
Why? What for?

70
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:29,348
What do you mean, why?

71
00:06:29,431 --> 00:06:31,225
I'll say it again, Ana.

72
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:33,268
People are talking.

73
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:36,438
Everyone's already talking
about what happened at the café.

74
00:06:36,522 --> 00:06:39,149
What if they find out
about the scene at my house?

75
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:41,193
They won't find out.

76
00:06:42,236 --> 00:06:46,990
Ana, that woman
walked out of my house unscathed.

77
00:06:47,407 --> 00:06:49,993
You and your husband
did nothing about it.

78
00:06:50,494 --> 00:06:53,080
I'm sure that woman will keep coming back

79
00:06:53,163 --> 00:06:54,540
to cause a scene.

80
00:06:54,623 --> 00:06:56,542
And I will deal with her every time.

81
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,043
But please, Ma...

82
00:06:59,086 --> 00:07:01,296
please stay out of it, okay?

83
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:05,676
You take care.

84
00:07:16,645 --> 00:07:19,064
I'll call someone to fix the window.

85
00:07:19,148 --> 00:07:21,817
Regina will never admit that she broke it.

86
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:26,071
These past few days,
she's been making up a lot of stories.

87
00:07:29,283 --> 00:07:31,326
How did you get to my office?

88
00:07:37,708 --> 00:07:39,042
I found a way.

89
00:07:39,626 --> 00:07:41,211
You weren't answering my calls.

90
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:45,048
Don't ever do that again.

91
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:51,471
Ben, I wouldn't have had to do that
if you had answered my calls.

92
00:07:56,643 --> 00:07:58,729
I'm leaving.

93
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:00,189
Hey, Ben, hold on.

94
00:08:01,356 --> 00:08:03,192
You're leaving Regina again?

95
00:08:03,734 --> 00:08:05,819
You leave whenever she's calm.

96
00:08:05,903 --> 00:08:07,905
And you're never here when she needs you.

97
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:09,448
Mara.

98
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:14,369
I can't stay here long

99
00:08:15,329 --> 00:08:17,080
because I have a life of my own.

100
00:08:17,915 --> 00:08:18,999
And I don't?

101
00:08:20,292 --> 00:08:21,793
You have a job.

102
00:08:23,295 --> 00:08:26,048
Your job is to take care of my sister.

103
00:08:28,050 --> 00:08:30,302
Or is something else keeping you busy?

104
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:33,013
Hmm?

105
00:08:37,142 --> 00:08:38,435
What do you mean?

106
00:08:38,936 --> 00:08:40,062
I don't know.

107
00:08:41,146 --> 00:08:42,397
You tell me.

108
00:08:44,399 --> 00:08:46,068
Just say it to my face, Ben.

109
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:47,527
What are you implying?

110
00:08:50,364 --> 00:08:52,157
Do you smoke, Mara?

111
00:08:56,370 --> 00:08:57,454
Okay.

112
00:08:58,163 --> 00:09:00,582
Yes. What's wrong with that?

113
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:05,045
You didn't even tell me.

114
00:09:07,214 --> 00:09:08,632
And...

115
00:09:08,715 --> 00:09:11,385
if you could hide something
that's not a big deal,

116
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:15,305
you're probably hiding
something even bigger.

117
00:09:17,474 --> 00:09:19,726
You're scared of your own shadow.

118
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:25,023
Watch over my sister.

119
00:09:25,107 --> 00:09:27,109
I'm paying you to do your job.

120
00:09:27,192 --> 00:09:29,528
All you care about is money, huh?

121
00:09:32,155 --> 00:09:34,574
So, what is it you want, Mara?

122
00:09:35,409 --> 00:09:36,994
I'm getting tired, Ben.

123
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:40,414
There'll come a day
when your money won't be enough

124
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:42,457
for everything I'm doing.

125
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:45,460
What exactly is your plan here?

126
00:09:45,544 --> 00:09:46,878
Do you even have a plan?

127
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:50,799
Is your plan
to just lock up your sister forever?

128
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:54,052
Mara, there are things
you don't understand.

129
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:59,266
My sister will be part of my life
at the right time.

130
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,019
- Ben.
- Take care of my sister.

131
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:04,688
It's your sister
we're talking about here, Ben!

132
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,868
I'm so annoyed with Brian.

133
00:10:19,244 --> 00:10:20,871
He didn't want to let me go.

134
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,956
He has a lot of problems in...

135
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:24,750
his personal life.

136
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,502
He no longer does his job
at the firm properly.

137
00:10:28,337 --> 00:10:31,340
I'm sorry I had to go,
and I couldn't come back.

138
00:10:36,928 --> 00:10:38,347
So, what happened?

139
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:45,645
People are talking about me, Ben.

140
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,651
About what happened to Beth and me...

141
00:10:51,735 --> 00:10:53,153
in the café.

142
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:57,741
Yeah, I heard them.

143
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:00,952
You heard them?

144
00:11:01,036 --> 00:11:02,954
The people gossiping about it.

145
00:11:03,038 --> 00:11:04,247
And then?

146
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,042
What did you do?

147
00:11:09,336 --> 00:11:10,670
What do you mean?

148
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:14,758
What do I mean?

149
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:18,053
What did you do?

150
00:11:19,763 --> 00:11:21,098
You didn't do anything?

151
00:11:21,932 --> 00:11:24,768
Is it because you agree with them
that I'm in the wrong?

152
00:11:25,477 --> 00:11:27,479
She attacked me.

153
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:28,980
She slapped me first.

154
00:11:29,064 --> 00:11:31,066
I am the victim.

155
00:11:32,109 --> 00:11:35,445
Ben! I am your wife.

156
00:11:36,446 --> 00:11:37,948
I know that, Ana.

157
00:11:38,782 --> 00:11:40,200
And I'm on your side.

158
00:11:41,243 --> 00:11:44,329
It's just that... that was a work event.

159
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:48,417
How could I argue with the people there?

160
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,212
We better go to sleep.

161
00:11:53,505 --> 00:11:55,340
Ana...

162
00:11:55,424 --> 00:11:58,844
We need to be early tomorrow.
We'll have breakfast with Mom.

163
00:12:02,514 --> 00:12:04,683
Benjamin deserves that award.

164
00:12:04,766 --> 00:12:06,977
I even wonder why they just gave it now.

165
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,563
He has done so much for the <i>azucarera</i>

166
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:12,190
and for the people here in Vallente.

167
00:12:12,274 --> 00:12:16,069
It sounds like you want Attorney Ben
to run in the next election.

168
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,822
Ladies,
let's not get ahead of ourselves, okay?

169
00:12:20,157 --> 00:12:22,159
Oh! Speaking of.

170
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:24,578
- Ana! Hello.
- Hi, Ma.

171
00:12:24,661 --> 00:12:26,580
- Hello, everyone.
- Hi, Ben!

172
00:12:27,164 --> 00:12:28,373
Mom, I didn't know you had a meeting.

173
00:12:28,457 --> 00:12:30,876
You could've just called me
to say what you had to say.

174
00:12:30,959 --> 00:12:32,461
Ugh, don't be silly.

175
00:12:32,961 --> 00:12:35,422
This is why I asked you to come here.

176
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:36,673
- Is this for us?
- Yes.

177
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:38,216
Nanny, put it in the kitchen.

178
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:39,718
Thank you so much.

179
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:43,638
Attorney Ben will be awarded
as this year's Child of Visayas.

180
00:12:43,722 --> 00:12:48,602
It is to acknowledge
your work and dedication to our community.

181
00:12:49,436 --> 00:12:51,021
Congratulations.

182
00:12:52,856 --> 00:12:53,773
Are you sure?

183
00:12:55,358 --> 00:12:56,943
- Wow.
- Ben.

184
00:12:57,027 --> 00:12:59,529
Do you think we joke about this thing?

185
00:13:00,197 --> 00:13:03,700
The Child of Visayas
is a very prestigious award.

186
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,410
Yes, of course we're sure.

187
00:13:05,494 --> 00:13:09,331
You'll need
to prepare a speech for the ceremony.

188
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:12,751
You wouldn't reject Vallente, would you?

189
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:14,794
Of course not.

190
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:17,923
Uh, thank you.

191
00:13:18,006 --> 00:13:21,593
I will have this arranged
with my secretary.

192
00:13:21,676 --> 00:13:23,970
- Perfect!
- Thank you.

193
00:13:24,054 --> 00:13:26,473
Benjamin, I am so proud of you.

194
00:13:26,556 --> 00:13:29,059
Congratulations to both of you.

195
00:13:29,476 --> 00:13:31,228
I'm so happy!

196
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:34,856
Nanny,
please keep this for Mom.

197
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:37,901
And then, you can serve this
to those she's meeting with.

198
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:41,321
All right, keep that.
I'll handle this myself.

199
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:46,743
Ana, dear.

200
00:13:54,834 --> 00:13:56,545
I wanted to...

201
00:13:57,879 --> 00:14:01,132
congratulate you and Ben for your award.

202
00:14:02,092 --> 00:14:04,010
You should say that to him instead.

203
00:14:07,889 --> 00:14:10,141
I know I've told you that...

204
00:14:10,934 --> 00:14:12,936
you shouldn't put up with your husband.

205
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:19,442
I was wrong.

206
00:14:22,696 --> 00:14:24,781
I've realized you're a wife

207
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:28,243
who won't easily lose
your love for your husband.

208
00:14:29,744 --> 00:14:31,830
That's why that award is for both of you.

209
00:14:34,332 --> 00:14:37,836
I know Ben wouldn't do
what people said he did...

210
00:14:39,045 --> 00:14:42,048
if you hadn't supported him
in everything he does.

211
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:46,970
That's why Ben is very lucky to have you.

212
00:14:54,811 --> 00:14:56,062
Thank you.

213
00:14:58,315 --> 00:14:59,399
Dad.

214
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:08,950
My child, may I hug you
just for a moment?

215
00:15:47,364 --> 00:15:49,032
Ben and I are heading out now.

216
00:15:49,115 --> 00:15:50,742
We still have work to do.

217
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:56,331
Take care, dear, okay?

218
00:16:00,502 --> 00:16:01,670
<i>Go, why not?</i>

219
00:16:01,753 --> 00:16:05,173
You're not new
to fashion fundraisers, right?

220
00:16:05,256 --> 00:16:08,968
Yeah, but after everything
that's happening, I...

221
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:13,431
I don't know, but I just want
to keep a low profile for now.

222
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:18,478
It's not surprising
that Attorney Ben has a mistress.

223
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:22,065
He's handsome and smart.
A lot of people will want him.

224
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:24,818
Maybe Ana isn't looking after him well.

225
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:27,320
Why can't she look after him
when they don't even have kids?

226
00:16:27,404 --> 00:16:29,155
It's just the two of them, right?

227
00:16:29,239 --> 00:16:31,658
Perhaps it's Attorney
who is taking care of Ana.

228
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:34,869
Her family has a history
of mental health issues, right?

229
00:16:34,953 --> 00:16:37,372
So, maybe Attorney
really has gotten tired of her.

230
00:16:37,455 --> 00:16:38,790
That's why he looked for someone else.

231
00:16:38,873 --> 00:16:41,042
- Kat, Kat! No, Kat!
- What the hell?

232
00:16:41,126 --> 00:16:42,377
- What the hell?
- No! Kat...

233
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:44,087
What-- They are talking nonsense!

234
00:16:44,170 --> 00:16:46,589
Kat, no, it's not worth it. Stop.

235
00:16:48,466 --> 00:16:50,135
We should have said something

236
00:16:50,218 --> 00:16:52,971
to put an end
to people gossiping about you.

237
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,766
Ana?

238
00:16:59,269 --> 00:17:00,687
I can't help it.

239
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:03,148
I don't want
to be affected anymore, but...

240
00:17:03,231 --> 00:17:04,482
I can't stop myself.

241
00:17:06,109 --> 00:17:07,944
So, you need to do something about it.

242
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:10,488
And what? Argue with them?

243
00:17:10,572 --> 00:17:13,241
No.
You need to redeem yourself.

244
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:15,452
Why?

245
00:17:15,535 --> 00:17:16,995
Why would I have to redeem myself

246
00:17:17,078 --> 00:17:19,080
if I didn't do anything wrong?

247
00:17:19,414 --> 00:17:21,249
I know, and I agree with you.

248
00:17:21,708 --> 00:17:24,544
But not everyone thinks the same way.

249
00:17:24,627 --> 00:17:27,297
In their eyes, you are in the wrong.

250
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:44,981
Hands?

251
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:51,613
So, I said yes to a fundraiser.

252
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:54,783
- Yeah?
- For Vallente Orphanage.

253
00:17:54,866 --> 00:17:55,950
- Wow!
- Yeah.

254
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:58,036
They're going to exhibit my designs.

255
00:17:58,119 --> 00:17:59,996
Wow, that's great!

256
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:03,166
Wow, so more people
are gonna see your work.

257
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:06,503
- Mm-hmm.
- I'm so happy to hear that.

258
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:08,213
Good job.

259
00:18:08,296 --> 00:18:10,715
- Thank you.
- I'm proud of you.

260
00:18:13,468 --> 00:18:15,303
- Okay.
- Thank you so much.

261
00:18:16,221 --> 00:18:18,640
Ana, Attorney, they're here.

262
00:18:18,723 --> 00:18:20,975
- Okay, Nanny.
- Thank you, Nanny.

263
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:24,771
- Okay? Thank you very much. Let's go.
- Yes.

264
00:18:29,442 --> 00:18:30,944
Bridge, let's just talk later.

265
00:18:31,027 --> 00:18:33,071
<i>Wait, why are you so hard to contact?</i>

266
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:36,074
<i>What "important thing"</i>
<i>are you doing now, Beth?</i>

267
00:18:37,325 --> 00:18:39,828
I said let's just talk later.

268
00:18:39,911 --> 00:18:41,162
Hey, Beth!

269
00:18:55,927 --> 00:18:59,264
I worked a lot of jobs
in Recto back then.

270
00:18:59,764 --> 00:19:01,057
Um...

271
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:04,978
I worked as a porter.
I sold an assortment of stuff.

272
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:06,563
I worked as a pedicab driver.

273
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,857
Until eventually,

274
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:12,360
I had the chance to be a...

275
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:15,154
service crew at a small restaurant.

276
00:19:15,238 --> 00:19:17,574
So, my salary increased then.

277
00:19:17,657 --> 00:19:20,159
That was when I was starting college.

278
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:25,748
I can't seem to imagine
you doing those jobs, Attorney.

279
00:19:26,916 --> 00:19:29,752
We knew you in Vallente
as Attorney Ben already.

280
00:19:29,836 --> 00:19:33,047
And now, the Child of Visayas awardee.

281
00:19:33,131 --> 00:19:34,674
Oh, that's true.

282
00:19:34,757 --> 00:19:37,760
I went through a lot
before I became a lawyer.

283
00:19:38,344 --> 00:19:40,346
Good times, tough times.

284
00:19:40,430 --> 00:19:43,474
But thanks to my...

285
00:19:43,558 --> 00:19:45,435
very beautiful and loving wife...

286
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:49,147
and everyone who supported me, I'm here.

287
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:52,567
Even though you're from Recto,

288
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:56,237
the people you really helped
are those here in Vallente.

289
00:19:59,157 --> 00:20:01,743
People think that...

290
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,954
I have a foundation.

291
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:07,040
Um...

292
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,625
But you know...

293
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:14,047
The <i>azucarera </i>and I,
we try to help others from outside.

294
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:17,926
But we know, Attorney,
not all are your fans.

295
00:20:18,009 --> 00:20:20,011
You said you're an open book.

296
00:20:20,094 --> 00:20:22,096
Rumor has it

297
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,349
that you and your wife
are having problems.

298
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:28,895
Oh, my God.

299
00:20:28,978 --> 00:20:31,481
No, that's not true.

300
00:20:33,066 --> 00:20:35,068
So, there's no third party?

301
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:36,819
"Third party"?

302
00:20:36,903 --> 00:20:39,155
- Yes.
- Third party.

303
00:20:41,866 --> 00:20:42,784
No, that's not true.

304
00:20:42,867 --> 00:20:44,535
There's no third party.

305
00:20:44,869 --> 00:20:46,037
Um...

306
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:48,915
My wife and I,
we're very okay,

307
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:52,335
because if we weren't,
my <i>barong</i> would've been a mess today.

308
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:57,215
She prepared this <i>barong</i> for me.

309
00:20:57,632 --> 00:20:59,717
But I'll tell you something,
you know...

310
00:21:00,385 --> 00:21:02,387
We're a normal married couple.

311
00:21:02,929 --> 00:21:04,764
- You know what I mean?
- Yeah.

312
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:08,017
We argue,
but we always talk things through.

313
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:08,935
Mm.

314
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:13,439
But to say we're drifting apart,

315
00:21:13,523 --> 00:21:16,609
or that there's a "third party,"

316
00:21:16,693 --> 00:21:19,946
or that I don't love my wife anymore?

317
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:23,825
That will never happen.

318
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:28,830
Well, straight from Attorney Ben himself.

319
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:30,540
It couldn't be any clearer.

320
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:34,127
So, we want to know more
about your bagasse project...

321
00:21:34,836 --> 00:21:36,337
It was nice having you over.

322
00:21:36,421 --> 00:21:37,839
Yes, thank you for having me.

323
00:21:37,922 --> 00:21:39,882
And thank you for the delicious snacks.

324
00:21:39,966 --> 00:21:41,384
Oh, my gosh, it's nothing.

325
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,219
- I'm glad you liked it.
- Thank you.

326
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,679
Are you sure we covered everything?

327
00:21:44,762 --> 00:21:45,763
- Yes, definitely, Attorney.
- Okay.

328
00:21:45,847 --> 00:21:47,849
- Thank you so much.
- All right, see you soon!

329
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:49,434
- See you! I'll go ahead.
- Thank you, thank you.

330
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:50,601
- All right.
- Bye.

331
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:52,687
Hey.

332
00:21:53,062 --> 00:21:54,605
That was a lot.

333
00:21:54,689 --> 00:21:55,940
You did well.

334
00:21:56,024 --> 00:21:57,692
Thank you. Thank you very much.

335
00:22:01,154 --> 00:22:03,156
Tired?

336
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:05,783
- Get some rest.
- Okay.

337
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:13,166
Ben!

338
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:15,793
Oh. Hello!

339
00:22:17,587 --> 00:22:18,755
Brian.

340
00:22:19,714 --> 00:22:22,300
Ben.
I hope you don't mind my sudden visit.

341
00:22:23,509 --> 00:22:25,011
No, of course not.

342
00:22:25,094 --> 00:22:26,512
- Of course not.
- Mm-hmm.

343
00:22:26,596 --> 00:22:27,805
- What's up?
- Ana.

344
00:22:27,889 --> 00:22:29,891
- Good to see you again.
- Hello.

345
00:22:29,974 --> 00:22:31,059
Yeah, we met at the party.

346
00:22:31,142 --> 00:22:32,643
- Thank you again. And...
- Yes.

347
00:22:32,727 --> 00:22:34,937
I heard you were together at the launch?

348
00:22:35,021 --> 00:22:36,439
Yeah.

349
00:22:38,149 --> 00:22:39,650
- How are you?
- Uh...

350
00:22:39,734 --> 00:22:42,987
I heard you're going through something.

351
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:44,822
Yeah.

352
00:22:44,906 --> 00:22:46,449
Ah, yes. Yeah...

353
00:22:46,532 --> 00:22:49,035
Actually, I am going through something
right now.

354
00:22:49,535 --> 00:22:51,204
Thanks for asking.

355
00:22:53,790 --> 00:22:55,124
Anyway, uh...

356
00:22:55,208 --> 00:22:58,211
Ana, would it be okay if I borrowed
your husband for a quick minute?

357
00:22:58,294 --> 00:23:00,171
I just need to talk to him
about something.

358
00:23:00,254 --> 00:23:01,589
Oh, okay, okay.

359
00:23:01,839 --> 00:23:03,257
So, um...

360
00:23:04,175 --> 00:23:05,760
I'll leave you two alone.

361
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:09,222
- Okay.
- Okay.

362
00:23:12,517 --> 00:23:15,019
Brian, sorry I never got back to you
the other day.

363
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:17,522
You were saying you're short?

364
00:23:20,358 --> 00:23:23,528
Mr. CEO,
you've been up to something

365
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:26,614
behind your wife's back again,
haven't you? Tsk, tsk.

366
00:23:27,115 --> 00:23:28,950
- What?
- You.

367
00:23:30,076 --> 00:23:32,578
You've been using me
as your excuse with your wife.

368
00:23:33,079 --> 00:23:35,331
That means

369
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:39,293
there's something
she isn't supposed to know.

370
00:23:41,003 --> 00:23:42,171
Am I right?

371
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:50,012
Okay.

372
00:23:51,097 --> 00:23:53,349
All right, Brian. How much do you need?

373
00:23:58,729 --> 00:24:00,815
I was going to ask for one million.

374
00:24:02,316 --> 00:24:04,235
But I changed my mind.

375
00:24:05,611 --> 00:24:07,613
Three million.

376
00:24:18,666 --> 00:24:19,667
What?

377
00:24:20,501 --> 00:24:24,839
I'm asking you for three million, Mr. CEO.

378
00:24:26,757 --> 00:24:28,968
- Yeah?
- You're serious?

379
00:24:30,928 --> 00:24:34,015
You show up at my house
to borrow money? No, I'm sorry.

380
00:24:34,098 --> 00:24:35,975
You're asking me for three million?

381
00:24:36,392 --> 00:24:38,311
It's this simple, Ben.

382
00:24:39,187 --> 00:24:42,940
Three million for my silence.

383
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:44,901
Because...

384
00:24:45,610 --> 00:24:48,613
I know things, Ben.

385
00:24:50,323 --> 00:24:51,657
You know things?

386
00:24:53,367 --> 00:24:57,788
Things that could bring you down, Mr. CEO.

387
00:25:00,583 --> 00:25:02,001
I know everything.

388
00:25:02,084 --> 00:25:05,338
Everything!

389
00:25:07,173 --> 00:25:08,841
Maybe you've forgotten...

390
00:25:09,342 --> 00:25:11,177
we move in the same circles.

391
00:25:12,762 --> 00:25:16,432
One post from me on social media,
and the news will spread fast.

392
00:25:16,515 --> 00:25:18,017
People will start asking questions.

393
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:19,310
Oh, my God.

394
00:25:19,894 --> 00:25:21,896
Especially in this town of Vallente,

395
00:25:22,438 --> 00:25:25,274
where everyone thinks so highly of you.

396
00:25:31,822 --> 00:25:32,865
Fine.

397
00:25:33,950 --> 00:25:35,284
Three million.

398
00:25:38,663 --> 00:25:40,331
Of course you'll give it to me.

399
00:25:40,414 --> 00:25:41,582
Of course.

400
00:25:42,083 --> 00:25:43,918
What's three million

401
00:25:44,001 --> 00:25:47,838
compared to the life
you're trying to protect, Mr. CEO?

402
00:25:52,510 --> 00:25:55,263
But I can't give it to you
right now, okay?

403
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:58,391
I'll fix it.

404
00:25:59,267 --> 00:26:00,518
I'll call you.

405
00:26:02,561 --> 00:26:05,648
Okay. I'll take your word for it.

406
00:26:07,942 --> 00:26:09,944
I'll wait for your call, Mr. Big Shot.

407
00:27:03,289 --> 00:27:04,332
Thank you.

408
00:27:06,250 --> 00:27:07,293
Hey.

409
00:27:07,793 --> 00:27:09,962
Thanks for helping me with the interview.

410
00:27:10,463 --> 00:27:11,797
Thank you.

411
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:15,718
You didn't have to
put the spotlight on me earlier.

412
00:27:15,801 --> 00:27:18,220
No, I want to.

413
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:24,352
And I wouldn't be here
if it weren't for you.

414
00:27:26,437 --> 00:27:28,439
Everything I do is for you, Ana.

415
00:27:37,114 --> 00:27:38,366
Good night.

416
00:27:38,991 --> 00:27:40,242
Okay, good night.

417
00:27:52,713 --> 00:27:53,714
Hey.

418
00:27:55,174 --> 00:27:57,343
I hope you have a good sleep tonight.

419
00:30:17,233 --> 00:30:19,568
Ben, do you have my money?

420
00:30:19,652 --> 00:30:21,070
Oh, there's nothing there.

421
00:30:21,153 --> 00:30:22,863
I was gonna offer you my yacht.

422
00:30:22,947 --> 00:30:25,199
- No.
- Would you like a yacht?

423
00:30:25,282 --> 00:30:26,825
You want to see it?
It's not far from here.

424
00:30:26,909 --> 00:30:28,327
It's really nice.

425
00:30:32,873 --> 00:30:34,542
Ben, do you or do you not have my money?

426
00:30:35,125 --> 00:30:36,460
Hand it over!

427
00:30:39,004 --> 00:30:40,005
Okay.

428
00:30:42,091 --> 00:30:43,092
I don't have it.

429
00:30:43,175 --> 00:30:44,593
What?

430
00:30:44,677 --> 00:30:47,096
The money's not here,
it's on the yacht.

431
00:30:47,179 --> 00:30:50,266
Brian, do you expect me
to bring three million pesos with me?

432
00:30:50,349 --> 00:30:51,392
Ben, do you understand me?

433
00:30:51,475 --> 00:30:54,228
I don't want your goddamn yacht!

434
00:30:54,311 --> 00:30:56,689
- Give me my money. Give me the money.
- It's on the yacht.

435
00:30:56,772 --> 00:30:58,232
Brian, you're not listening.

436
00:30:58,315 --> 00:31:00,109
The money is on the yacht.

437
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,361
Ben, no matter how hard
you push your yacht down my throat,

438
00:31:02,444 --> 00:31:03,487
you won't convince me.

439
00:31:03,571 --> 00:31:06,907
Just give me my money.
Give me my three million pesos.

440
00:31:06,991 --> 00:31:08,993
Brian, listen.

441
00:31:09,076 --> 00:31:10,828
The money isn't here,
it's on the yacht.

442
00:31:10,911 --> 00:31:13,372
What? Ben, are you deaf or dumb?

443
00:31:13,455 --> 00:31:15,332
I don't want your yacht!

444
00:31:15,416 --> 00:31:18,419
I am not going to your goddamn yacht!

445
00:31:18,502 --> 00:31:20,129
Give me my three million.

446
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:23,048
Brian, I told you,
the money is on the yacht.

447
00:31:23,132 --> 00:31:24,633
I don't have it with me.

448
00:31:24,717 --> 00:31:27,636
Ben-- Let me remind you.

449
00:31:30,097 --> 00:31:32,182
Are you going to give me the money,

450
00:31:32,266 --> 00:31:36,478
or do you want me to tell everyone I know
about your secrets?

451
00:31:38,105 --> 00:31:39,565
Brian,
I really don't have the money here.

452
00:31:39,648 --> 00:31:41,650
- No, no, no.
- It's on the yacht.

453
00:31:41,734 --> 00:31:44,069
Just answer the fucking question.

454
00:31:44,695 --> 00:31:46,447
Of course I'll give you your money.

455
00:31:46,530 --> 00:31:48,198
It's on the yacht!

456
00:31:48,282 --> 00:31:49,283
Let's go!

457
00:31:51,035 --> 00:31:52,703
You're really pushing my buttons, huh?

458
00:31:52,786 --> 00:31:55,289
Fine. You'll regret this.

459
00:31:55,372 --> 00:31:57,791
No, no, no, Brian, Brian.
Please, please, please don't.

460
00:31:59,209 --> 00:32:00,711
You bastard!

461
00:32:00,794 --> 00:32:02,046
Damn it-- Ben!

462
00:32:54,723 --> 00:32:56,350
I said let me go!

463
00:33:05,192 --> 00:33:06,193
You?

464
00:33:14,034 --> 00:33:16,203
Please let me go, ma'am.

465
00:33:16,286 --> 00:33:17,621
This is kidnapping--

466
00:33:23,127 --> 00:33:25,462
If Ben finds out--

467
00:33:28,132 --> 00:33:29,216
Go ahead.

468
00:33:29,925 --> 00:33:32,094
Keep talking.

469
00:33:32,636 --> 00:33:35,431
I'll make your cheeks swell up like hell.

470
00:33:35,931 --> 00:33:39,601
Now leave my daughter's husband alone.

471
00:33:41,979 --> 00:33:45,733
You have no idea
how crazy I can get for my daughter.

472
00:33:46,567 --> 00:33:47,651
Yes.

473
00:33:48,402 --> 00:33:50,904
I am doing this for my daughter.

474
00:33:51,905 --> 00:33:54,241
Because I don't want her life
to be ruined.

475
00:33:58,370 --> 00:34:02,624
I'm not the one who's destroying her life.

476
00:34:06,462 --> 00:34:09,131
You know, no matter what you say,

477
00:34:10,507 --> 00:34:13,427
you are still a homewrecker.

478
00:34:14,511 --> 00:34:15,929
I know your kind.

479
00:34:17,890 --> 00:34:21,477
Because I once made
the mistake of begging for my husband.

480
00:34:22,186 --> 00:34:24,188
But what did you do?

481
00:34:24,271 --> 00:34:25,939
You ruined me!

482
00:34:27,191 --> 00:34:30,778
Too bad for you.

483
00:34:31,487 --> 00:34:35,741
You'll be punished
for all the things others did to me.

484
00:34:37,701 --> 00:34:40,537
I have so much time in my hands.

485
00:34:42,039 --> 00:34:46,001
And I have a lot of things in my mind
that I can do to you.

486
00:34:48,587 --> 00:34:50,964
Your family will be blamed

487
00:34:51,048 --> 00:34:52,925
if I disappear--

488
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:59,807
That mouth of yours is so annoying!

489
00:35:09,066 --> 00:35:10,275
You know what?

490
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:13,779
Even if I let you go,

491
00:35:14,530 --> 00:35:16,824
you know what'll happen, right?

492
00:35:17,866 --> 00:35:19,451
You're a physical therapist, aren't you?

493
00:35:19,535 --> 00:35:23,372
So you know what'll happen
if your bones break.

494
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:30,712
For the last time,

495
00:35:31,922 --> 00:35:35,300
stay away from my daughter's husband.

496
00:35:35,384 --> 00:35:36,635
Do you understand?

497
00:35:36,718 --> 00:35:37,803
If you don't,

498
00:35:38,470 --> 00:35:40,973
I will do much worse things to you.

499
00:35:41,056 --> 00:35:42,599
Do I make myself clear?

500
00:35:43,976 --> 00:35:45,811
Do I make myself clear?

501
00:35:45,894 --> 00:35:47,646
Do I make myself clear?

502
00:35:48,397 --> 00:35:49,398
Answer me!

503
00:35:52,192 --> 00:35:53,443
I know.

504
00:35:58,699 --> 00:36:00,367
You bitch!

505
00:36:06,748 --> 00:36:08,375
Oh, my goodness...

506
00:36:12,129 --> 00:36:13,171
Let's go.

507
00:37:14,566 --> 00:37:16,777
<i>I am warning you, Beth.</i>

508
00:37:17,319 --> 00:37:19,905
<i>I can do unexplainable, crazy things</i>

509
00:37:19,988 --> 00:37:21,990
<i>for my daughter's love.</i>

510
00:37:28,121 --> 00:37:29,039
The heck?

511
00:37:29,122 --> 00:37:32,167
What is this mess? Nanny!

512
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:35,337
Clean up this mess! Oh, my God!

513
00:38:06,201 --> 00:38:07,536
What's this?

514
00:38:08,537 --> 00:38:10,747
Dinner... for you.

515
00:38:11,415 --> 00:38:13,542
The staff helped.

516
00:38:13,625 --> 00:38:15,335
But I cooked everything.

517
00:38:17,379 --> 00:38:19,631
What stupidity is this?

518
00:38:20,590 --> 00:38:22,634
It's just for tonight.

519
00:38:22,718 --> 00:38:24,052
This is all for you.

520
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:27,055
Look, Reynaldo.

521
00:38:27,139 --> 00:38:30,559
If I wanted a candlelit dinner,
I would've told the staff.

522
00:38:30,642 --> 00:38:31,560
And besides,

523
00:38:31,935 --> 00:38:34,938
why would I want to share
this kind of dinner with you?

524
00:38:35,856 --> 00:38:38,275
It's too late for this kind of nonsense!

525
00:38:47,117 --> 00:38:49,286
Happy anniversary, ma'am!

526
00:38:49,369 --> 00:38:50,871
Anniversary?

527
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:54,142
- I'm going, Ben.
- Huh?

528
00:39:54,226 --> 00:39:56,019
- I don't--
- Where are you going?

529
00:39:56,103 --> 00:39:58,563
Hey, sit down.

530
00:39:59,189 --> 00:40:01,942
- Ben...
- Sit down, Brian.

531
00:40:02,025 --> 00:40:04,194
- Come-- Brian, Brian, Brian.
- Let me go!

532
00:40:04,277 --> 00:40:05,862
Brian, Brian.

533
00:40:05,946 --> 00:40:06,905
It's okay. It's okay.

534
00:40:06,988 --> 00:40:08,490
- Let go of me!
- It's okay.

535
00:40:08,573 --> 00:40:09,783
I said it's okay.

536
00:40:19,209 --> 00:40:20,210
Fuck.

537
00:40:24,631 --> 00:40:27,300
Look what you did.
Now I have to clean this mess.

538
00:40:27,384 --> 00:40:29,010
- Huh?
- Please stop...

539
00:40:29,886 --> 00:40:30,971
What?

540
00:40:31,054 --> 00:40:32,889
What are you saying?

541
00:40:33,473 --> 00:40:34,474
What?

542
00:40:35,016 --> 00:40:37,227
You want me to stop?
Is that what you said?

543
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:38,687
You want me to stop?

544
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:39,980
Well, damn you.

545
00:40:40,689 --> 00:40:43,400
"Stop." Exactly.

546
00:40:43,483 --> 00:40:46,319
I've been asking you to do that.
I've asked you to stop.

547
00:40:46,403 --> 00:40:48,071
I didn't want to do this, either.

548
00:40:48,155 --> 00:40:50,282
That's why I'm here in Vallente, aren't I?

549
00:40:50,365 --> 00:40:52,951
Simply because I want to live in peace.

550
00:40:53,034 --> 00:40:55,871
But here you are, you damn bastard.

551
00:40:56,371 --> 00:40:57,789
You all want to destroy

552
00:40:57,873 --> 00:41:00,709
the things I've worked hard on.

553
00:41:00,792 --> 00:41:03,628
I just want to live a quiet life
with my wife, okay?

554
00:41:03,712 --> 00:41:05,422
I'm doing my job quietly.

555
00:41:05,505 --> 00:41:06,548
What were you planning to do?

556
00:41:06,631 --> 00:41:08,967
People like you are the ones
who make me do this.

557
00:41:09,050 --> 00:41:11,386
You're asking me
for three million pesos, huh?

558
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:12,762
Did you think I'd just give it to you?

559
00:41:12,846 --> 00:41:14,264
You thought you'd get it easily?

560
00:41:14,347 --> 00:41:15,515
Then you're damn wrong.

561
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:19,853
Fuck!

562
00:41:24,274 --> 00:41:25,358
Brian?

563
00:41:26,234 --> 00:41:27,068
Brian.

564
00:41:34,784 --> 00:41:35,785
Fuck!

565
00:43:12,632 --> 00:43:14,801
Ma'am Imelda!

566
00:43:16,469 --> 00:43:18,471
Ma'am Imelda! Ma'am Imelda!

567
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:22,767
- Oh, my goodness!
- Ma'am Imelda!

568
00:43:23,518 --> 00:43:25,687
I'm going to teach this kid a lesson.

569
00:43:25,770 --> 00:43:28,023
- Ma'am Imelda!
- Wait!

570
00:43:32,402 --> 00:43:35,155
What is it? You're so loud!

571
00:43:35,238 --> 00:43:37,615
What do you have to say
that you had to wake me up?

572
00:43:37,699 --> 00:43:39,284
Speak now!

573
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:44,039
Papa is gone.

574
00:44:03,808 --> 00:44:05,226
Miss Cedes?

575
00:44:06,019 --> 00:44:07,854
- Where's the coffee?
- Here, sir.

576
00:44:07,937 --> 00:44:10,565
Hand it here. Okay. I got it.

577
00:44:11,149 --> 00:44:12,484
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

578
00:44:23,078 --> 00:44:24,412
Good morning.

579
00:44:28,249 --> 00:44:29,584
Morning.

580
00:44:35,507 --> 00:44:36,674
Did you sleep well?

581
00:44:37,092 --> 00:44:39,511
- Mm-hmm.
- Good.

582
00:44:40,929 --> 00:44:42,097
I'm so happy.

583
00:44:43,598 --> 00:44:44,849
- Please, sit down.
- Yeah.

584
00:44:46,184 --> 00:44:47,769
Ah, Ana...

585
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:50,772
You should keep doing that.
Let your mind rest at night.

586
00:44:51,940 --> 00:44:53,441
To help you sleep well.

587
00:44:55,860 --> 00:44:57,112
Anyway,

588
00:44:57,195 --> 00:45:02,200
please enjoy your runny eggs
and soft bacon.

589
00:45:02,283 --> 00:45:03,410
Thank you.

590
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:11,459
Hello, Ma?

591
00:45:17,340 --> 00:45:19,175
Wha-what? What do you mean?

592
00:45:31,271 --> 00:45:33,189
Are you sure
the flowers are already in the chapel?

593
00:45:33,273 --> 00:45:34,232
Yes, ma'am.

594
00:45:34,315 --> 00:45:36,317
- What about the coffin?
- It's there.

595
00:45:36,401 --> 00:45:37,986
- Ma...
- Are you sure? Okay.

596
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:39,279
- Make sure to check everything.
- Okay, ma'am.

597
00:45:39,362 --> 00:45:41,781
Ma, it's okay.
What's happening?

598
00:45:41,865 --> 00:45:43,116
You know what's happening.

599
00:45:43,199 --> 00:45:46,369
I'm organizing
your father's burial, what else?

600
00:45:46,453 --> 00:45:47,787
- Ma...
- Would you like us to help?

601
00:45:48,246 --> 00:45:50,290
No need, Benjamin.
I can do it on my own.

602
00:45:50,373 --> 00:45:52,292
But if you want to help,
fine, suit yourself.

603
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:54,961
If you changed your mind,
you can just relax.

604
00:45:55,044 --> 00:45:56,713
Wait. Hey, come here.

605
00:45:56,796 --> 00:45:59,215
Where's the catering?
What happened to the catering?

606
00:45:59,299 --> 00:46:01,009
What time are they arriving?
They can't be late.

607
00:46:01,092 --> 00:46:02,594
- We can't serve spoiled food.
- Ma.

608
00:46:02,677 --> 00:46:04,053
It's embarrassing to the guests.

609
00:46:04,137 --> 00:46:05,638
- Ma.
- What?

610
00:46:05,722 --> 00:46:06,639
Slow down.

611
00:46:06,723 --> 00:46:08,016
Where is Juancho?

612
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:09,559
Juancho is in the morgue.

613
00:46:09,642 --> 00:46:12,020
He's taking care of your father.

614
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:13,521
- Hey! Come here.
- Yes, ma'am?

615
00:46:13,605 --> 00:46:14,898
- What are you still doing here?
- What is it?

616
00:46:14,981 --> 00:46:18,860
I told you to bring Reynaldo's clothes.
Why are you still here?

617
00:46:18,943 --> 00:46:20,320
I already did, ma'am.

618
00:46:20,403 --> 00:46:21,654
- Ma?
- Options.

619
00:46:21,738 --> 00:46:22,864
Give them options.

620
00:46:22,947 --> 00:46:24,699
- Hurry up! I still have a lot--
- Ma.

621
00:46:24,782 --> 00:46:26,576
Can you just...

622
00:46:26,659 --> 00:46:27,660
Ana, look.

623
00:46:27,744 --> 00:46:29,287
I am so busy, okay?

624
00:46:29,370 --> 00:46:31,164
I have so much to take care of!

625
00:46:31,623 --> 00:46:33,958
You know,
I want this wake to be fabulous.

626
00:46:34,042 --> 00:46:36,127
I'm sure a lot of people will come.

627
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:38,254
If you want to help, then help.
If you don't want to,

628
00:46:38,338 --> 00:46:42,217
take a seat, relax,
or do whatever you want!

629
00:46:42,300 --> 00:46:45,094
You! We should bring
the expensive glasses to the chapel,

630
00:46:45,178 --> 00:46:46,262
so they would look nice.

631
00:46:46,346 --> 00:46:47,639
It's okay.

632
00:46:47,722 --> 00:46:49,224
She's not okay.

633
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:52,560
Maybe it's her way of... coping.

634
00:46:55,230 --> 00:46:58,066
It's okay. Just let her.

635
00:47:01,861 --> 00:47:03,112
You should relax.

636
00:47:06,366 --> 00:47:08,535
I'm sorry for your loss, Imelda.

637
00:47:08,618 --> 00:47:09,661
Thank you.

638
00:47:14,958 --> 00:47:16,709
You're so lucky, Imelda.

639
00:47:16,793 --> 00:47:20,463
Even though Ana's husband is a CEO,
he's still helping out here.

640
00:47:22,090 --> 00:47:26,719
That's how much Ben loves my daughter.

641
00:47:27,804 --> 00:47:30,807
Ma'am, Madam Mona is here.

642
00:47:30,890 --> 00:47:31,975
Thank you.

643
00:47:32,684 --> 00:47:33,935
Excuse me for a second.

644
00:47:35,687 --> 00:47:38,940
Imelda.
Our deepest condolences.

645
00:47:40,692 --> 00:47:42,110
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

646
00:47:42,193 --> 00:47:43,444
We appreciate it.

647
00:47:45,113 --> 00:47:46,823
Last time...

648
00:47:46,906 --> 00:47:48,992
we were the ones
offering you our condolences.

649
00:47:49,492 --> 00:47:52,996
Imelda, we should stop meeting
in this kind of setting.

650
00:47:53,788 --> 00:47:54,789
I know.

651
00:47:55,206 --> 00:47:57,875
I'm glad
your granddaughter could join you.

652
00:47:59,002 --> 00:48:00,753
Surprisingly,

653
00:48:00,837 --> 00:48:02,255
she agreed to come.

654
00:48:07,635 --> 00:48:08,761
Come here.

655
00:48:10,054 --> 00:48:11,556
Do you want anything?

656
00:48:11,639 --> 00:48:12,765
- Do you want some drinks?
- No, thank you.

657
00:48:12,849 --> 00:48:14,601
I'll pay my respects first.

658
00:48:14,684 --> 00:48:16,269
- I'll accompany you.
- Ana, come with her.

659
00:48:24,193 --> 00:48:26,738
I'll only let you talk
to her granddaughter this time.

660
00:48:26,821 --> 00:48:27,739
Do you understand?

661
00:48:28,281 --> 00:48:30,617
- Get on with it.
- Thank you.

662
00:48:36,539 --> 00:48:37,707
Are you okay?

663
00:48:38,291 --> 00:48:40,043
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

664
00:48:40,835 --> 00:48:43,588
Let me handle this.
Ana said you haven't eaten yet.

665
00:48:44,714 --> 00:48:46,132
There's food in the room.

666
00:48:46,591 --> 00:48:47,675
Come on.

667
00:48:48,092 --> 00:48:49,177
Thank you.

668
00:48:54,349 --> 00:48:55,850
Please put it there.
Thank you.

669
00:48:58,102 --> 00:49:00,521
That's his son from another woman.

670
00:49:01,147 --> 00:49:03,316
I can't believe Imelda. She accepted him?

671
00:49:04,150 --> 00:49:05,985
She even prepared a beautiful wake

672
00:49:06,069 --> 00:49:09,030
for the man
who had cheated on her.

673
00:49:09,530 --> 00:49:11,282
Do you know the cause of death?

674
00:49:11,366 --> 00:49:14,911
It's probably because of stress
from what Ana did to Ben's mistress.

675
00:49:14,994 --> 00:49:18,039
Who wouldn't be stressed out by that?

676
00:49:18,122 --> 00:49:21,959
Especially when he learned
that his daughter connived

677
00:49:22,043 --> 00:49:26,005
with some woman to flirt with her husband.

678
00:49:26,089 --> 00:49:27,215
Hello.

679
00:49:27,298 --> 00:49:29,300
Do you believe in ghosts?

680
00:49:32,261 --> 00:49:34,597
Could you let me know
when the spirit of Ana's father

681
00:49:34,681 --> 00:49:36,099
pays you a visit

682
00:49:36,182 --> 00:49:39,686
because you keep on badmouthing her?

683
00:49:41,270 --> 00:49:42,271
But...

684
00:49:42,355 --> 00:49:46,526
please, just for your clarity,
let me say it myself, okay?

685
00:49:47,193 --> 00:49:48,444
The truth is...

686
00:49:49,445 --> 00:49:51,781
my wife didn't do anything wrong.

687
00:49:51,864 --> 00:49:53,533
And secondly...

688
00:49:55,535 --> 00:49:57,704
there's no other woman in my life...

689
00:49:59,038 --> 00:50:00,164
but...

690
00:50:00,998 --> 00:50:02,500
my loving wife.

691
00:50:12,176 --> 00:50:14,262
- Are you okay?
- Thank you.

692
00:50:33,197 --> 00:50:36,534
I hate you so much.

693
00:50:36,617 --> 00:50:38,453
I hate you.

694
00:50:40,163 --> 00:50:41,497
Oh, God.

695
00:50:41,581 --> 00:50:42,582
Oh, my God!

696
00:50:42,665 --> 00:50:44,333
Why am I crying?

697
00:50:44,751 --> 00:50:46,335
Why am I crying?

698
00:50:46,419 --> 00:50:47,378
Oh, my gosh.

699
00:50:47,462 --> 00:50:49,547
I want to go home, Juancho! Let's go!

700
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:50,965
Let's go! Hurry up!

701
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:52,800
Let's go.

702
00:50:52,884 --> 00:50:54,385
I can't stand it here.

703
00:51:03,311 --> 00:51:05,146
I thought I hated him too.

704
00:51:09,484 --> 00:51:11,152
Why does it hurt?

705
00:51:18,826 --> 00:51:20,411
Maybe you didn't hate him.

706
00:51:24,999 --> 00:51:26,918
You just hated the things he did.

707
00:54:20,383 --> 00:54:21,384
Ging.

708
00:54:21,842 --> 00:54:23,010
It's good.

709
00:54:28,724 --> 00:54:30,142
How did you get here?

710
00:54:39,485 --> 00:54:42,238


711
00:54:42,321 --> 00:54:43,280
<i>Ging.</i>

712
00:54:43,364 --> 00:54:44,740
- Hi. Good morning.
Ben.

713
00:54:45,366 --> 00:54:46,617
Good morning. Where were you?

714
00:54:46,701 --> 00:54:48,911
I did a morning walk. It starts outside.

715
00:54:49,495 --> 00:54:51,414
Let everyone enter!

716
00:54:51,497 --> 00:54:54,208
<i>We all admire</i>
<i>the Child of Visayas.</i>

717
00:54:54,291 --> 00:54:57,044
<i>- Attorney Benjamin Santos!</i>

718
00:54:58,879 --> 00:55:00,297
<i>Do you want to eat?</i>

719
00:55:04,093 --> 00:55:04,927
Yes.

720
00:55:05,011 --> 00:55:08,014
My brother killed my husband.
My brother killed my husband.

721
00:55:08,097 --> 00:55:10,057
- Regina.
My brother killed my husband.

722
00:55:10,766 --> 00:55:11,767
Did you see it?

723
00:55:12,184 --> 00:55:14,186
-

724
00:55:14,270 --> 00:55:17,940

<i>It's better to have a gun than a knife.</i>

725
00:55:19,358 --> 00:55:21,777

